From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:48:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] US: add the missing IMS APN for 310240 (Mint)

310240 carries six APN rows and not one of them is type=ims, so a Mint SIM has no IMS PDN to
attach to. 310260 -- T-Mobile proper, which this SIM registers on as an EHPLMN -- has eight, but
Android matches APNs on the SIM's own operator numeric, so none of them are reachable.

The visible effect is that imsdatadaemon never finishes starting: dsi_get_data_srvc_hndl for the IMS
ApnType finds nothing, so sys.ims.DATA_DAEMON_STATUS is never set and init never starts
ims_rtp_daemon. IMS registration itself succeeds -- it is the media path that is missing.

Mirrors the ungated 'T-Mobile US IMS' row, gated to Mint's gid the same way Mint's existing data row
is, so the other MVNOs sharing 310240 are unaffected.
---
 US.xml | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/US.xml b/US.xml
index 1802652..583d7ab 100644
--- a/US.xml
+++ b/US.xml
@@ -877,6 +877,20 @@
         roaming_protocol="IPV4V6"
         type="default,supl,mms,ia"
     />
+    <apn
+        mcc="310"
+        mnc="240"
+        carrier="Mint IMS"
+        apn="ims"
+        bearer_bitmask="14|18|20"
+        mtu="1440"
+        mvno_match_data="756D"
+        mvno_type="gid"
+        protocol="IPV6"
+        roaming_protocol="IPV4V6"
+        type="ims"
+        user_visible="false"
+    />
     <apn
         mcc="310"
         mnc="240"
